# XCU awk
# Copyright (c) 2026 Nicholas Martin. All rights reserved.
#
# All tests run in the POSIX locale. Focused on the options, variables,
# statements and functions the page defines; not an exhaustive grammar test.
# The standard input of every awk run that could read it is a pipe that ends
# or /dev/null.

assertion  XCU.awk.001
anchor     utilities/awk.html#OPTIONS/-F
anchor     utilities/awk.html#OPTIONS/-f
anchor     utilities/awk.html#OPTIONS/-v
class      required
since      1992
says       -F sepstring sets the field separator, -v assigns before BEGIN with escape processing, and several -f files are concatenated into one program (a - file being standard input).
test       t/001-options.sh

assertion  XCU.awk.002
anchor     utilities/awk.html#EXTENDED DESCRIPTION
anchor     utilities/awk.html#DESCRIPTION
class      required
since      1992
says       BEGIN actions run first in order, then each record is matched against every pattern in order, then END actions; a missing pattern matches all and a missing action prints the record; BEGIN-only programs read no input.
test       t/002-program-structure.sh

assertion  XCU.awk.003
anchor     utilities/awk.html#DESCRIPTION
anchor     utilities/awk.html#EXTENDED DESCRIPTION
class      required
since      1992
says       Records split into fields $1.., $0 is the record; assigning a field rebuilds $0 with OFS, assigning past the end extends NF, and reading a missing field creates none.
test       t/003-fields.sh

assertion  XCU.awk.004
anchor     utilities/awk.html#OPTIONS/-F
anchor     utilities/awk.html#EXTENDED DESCRIPTION
class      required
since      1992
says       FS of a blank splits on runs of blanks, another single character at each occurrence, longer values are EREs, and a new FS applies from the next record.
test       t/004-field-separator.sh

assertion  XCU.awk.005
anchor     utilities/awk.html#EXTENDED DESCRIPTION
anchor     utilities/awk.html#DESCRIPTION
class      required
since      1992
says       RS of one character ends records there; a null RS separates records at blank lines and makes newline a field separator.
test       t/005-record-separator.sh

assertion  XCU.awk.006
anchor     utilities/awk.html#EXTENDED DESCRIPTION
class      required
since      1992
says       NR, FNR, FILENAME, NF, OFS, ORS, OFMT, CONVFMT, SUBSEP, ENVIRON, ARGC, ARGV, RSTART and RLENGTH have the values and effects described.
test       t/006-special-variables.sh

assertion  XCU.awk.007
anchor     utilities/awk.html#OPERANDS
class      required
since      1992
says       A name=value operand assigns the variable just before the next file is read (after BEGIN, before END), with escapes processed and numeric-string typing.
test       t/007-assignment-operands.sh

assertion  XCU.awk.008
anchor     utilities/awk.html#EXTENDED DESCRIPTION
class      required
since      1992
says       Operators follow the stated precedence and associativity; conversions, Boolean contexts, increments, assignment operators, comparison rules, ~, in and concatenation behave as described.
test       t/008-expressions.sh

assertion  XCU.awk.009
anchor     utilities/awk.html#EXTENDED DESCRIPTION
class      required
since      1992
says       Arrays are associative with string subscripts; a list of subscripts is joined by SUBSEP; a reference creates an element but in does not; delete, for-in and split work as described.
test       t/009-arrays.sh

assertion  XCU.awk.010
anchor     utilities/awk.html#EXTENDED DESCRIPTION
anchor     utilities/awk.html#EXIT STATUS
class      required
since      1992
says       if, while, do-while, for, break, continue, next and exit behave as described; exit runs END actions and sets the status, and an exit inside END ends the program.
test       t/010-control-flow.sh

assertion  XCU.awk.011
anchor     utilities/awk.html#EXTENDED DESCRIPTION
class      required
since      1992
says       print and printf write to standard output, a truncated file, an appended file or a pipe, use OFS and ORS, and printf supports d, s, c, x, X, o, u, f, e, g, % with flags, width and precision (also from arguments).
test       t/011-output.sh

assertion  XCU.awk.012
anchor     utilities/awk.html#EXTENDED DESCRIPTION
class      required
since      1992
says       length, index, substr, sub, gsub (including & and its escape), sprintf, tolower and toupper return the specified values; sub and gsub act on $0 or a field and re-split.
test       t/012-string-functions.sh

assertion  XCU.awk.013
anchor     utilities/awk.html#EXTENDED DESCRIPTION
class      required
since      1992
says       int, sqrt, exp, log, sin, cos and atan2 return the specified values; srand sets a repeatable seed and returns the previous one, and rand returns values in [0,1).
test       t/013-math-functions.sh

assertion  XCU.awk.014
anchor     utilities/awk.html#EXTENDED DESCRIPTION
class      required
since      1992
says       getline in its forms reads the next record into $0 or a variable from the input, a file or a command, returning 1, 0 or -1 and updating NR, FNR and NF as described; close and system return statuses.
test       t/014-getline-and-system.sh

assertion  XCU.awk.015
anchor     utilities/awk.html#EXTENDED DESCRIPTION
class      required
since      1992
says       User-defined functions may be called before definition and recurse; extra parameters are locals; scalars pass by value and arrays by reference; return needs no value.
test       t/015-user-functions.sh

assertion  XCU.awk.016
anchor     utilities/awk.html#EXTENDED DESCRIPTION
class      required
since      1992
says       ERE constants and dynamic regular expressions follow the stated escapes; a bare /re/ tests $0; range patterns are inclusive, repeat, and run to the end if never closed.
test       t/016-regex-and-ranges.sh

assertion  XCU.awk.017
anchor     utilities/awk.html#EXTENDED DESCRIPTION
class      required
since      1992
says       Numeric-looking input from fields, getline, ARGV, ENVIRON, split, -v and operands compares as numbers, while string constants and concatenations compare as strings.
test       t/017-numeric-strings.sh

assertion  XCU.awk.018
anchor     utilities/awk.html#CONSEQUENCES OF ERRORS
anchor     utilities/awk.html#EXIT STATUS
class      required
since      1992
says       A file operand that cannot be accessed makes awk write a diagnostic, terminate without further action and exit above zero.
test       t/018-missing-file.sh

assertion  XCU.awk.019
anchor     utilities/awk.html#EXTENDED DESCRIPTION
class      required
since      2024
says       nextfile abandons the current file, fflush returns 0, and FILENAME is - for standard input.
test       t/019-later-additions.sh
